# Cloudinary + React — AI coding rules for apps/dashboard

Generated to mirror the `create-cloudinary-react` starter kit conventions and
this repo's AGENTS.md. These are authoritative for Cloudinary SDK usage in the
dashboard.

## Stack
- React 19 + Vite 6 + TypeScript 5 (strict). NOT Next.js.
- Server state via `@tanstack/react-query` only. No Redux.
- Maps via `maplibre-gl`.

## Cloudinary — imports and usage
- Build every delivery URL with `@cloudinary/url-gen`. Never hand-write a
  Cloudinary URL string.
  - Instance: `import { Cloudinary } from '@cloudinary/url-gen';`
    (see `src/cloudinary/config.ts` — reuse the shared `cld` export).
  - Image object: `cld.image(publicId)`.
  - Delivery: `import { format, quality } from '@cloudinary/url-gen/actions/delivery';`
    then `.delivery(format('auto')).delivery(quality('auto'))`.
  - Resize: `import { scale, fill } from '@cloudinary/url-gen/actions/resize';`
    then `.resize(scale().width(400))`.
- Render with the React SDK component, never a raw `<img>` with a guessed URL:
  - `import { AdvancedImage } from '@cloudinary/react';`
  - `<AdvancedImage cldImg={img} alt="..." />`
  - The local `CldImage` wrapper in `src/components/CldImage.tsx` wraps
    `AdvancedImage`; prefer it.
- Upload only via the unsigned widget in `src/cloudinary/UploadWidget.tsx`
  using the `verified_capture` preset.

## Security (non-negotiable — AGENTS.md §3.5, §3.11)
- Only `VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME` and `VITE_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET` are
  client-safe Cloudinary values.
- NEVER reference the Cloudinary API secret or API key in this app.
  They are server-only and would leak in the bundle.
- NEVER hand-roll Cloudinary signing. Signed delivery URLs are minted by the
  API (`@impact/api`); the client asks for a URL by `asset_id`, never by
  `public_id`.
- The client is untrusted. Never derive `org_id`/`user_id` from anything but the
  verified Supabase session.

## Common pitfalls to avoid
- Do not import `CldImage` from `next-cloudinary` — this is a Vite app. Use the
  local wrapper over `@cloudinary/react`.
- Do not mix up `@cloudinary/url-gen` (URL building) with `@cloudinary/react`
  (rendering). You need both.
- Do not query Cloudinary for product data. Postgres is the system of record.
